│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ none                                                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ The current ansatz uses 24 distinct parameters (nearly one per gate), which is expensive  │
│                          │ per the parameter-economy criterion and also likely drives the large train/validation gap │
│                          │ (0.88 vs 0.63) seen in the metrics — the circuit is overfitting the tiny training set. I  │
│                          │ restructure the ansatz to use aggressive parameter sharing: instead of a unique parameter │
│                          │ per qubit for each RY/RZ layer, I group qubits into two interleaved sets (even/odd) and   │
│                          │ share one parameter per gate-type per group. This cuts the parameter count from 24        │
│                          │ distinct names down to 6, while preserving the same gate structure/depth (still one RY    │
│                          │ layer, two RZ layers, and the CZ entangling chain), which should improve parameter        │
│                          │ efficiency and reduce the generalization gap since fewer degrees of freedom are available │
│                          │ to fit noise in the small training set. The entangling CZ layer stays fixed (no           │
│                          │ parameters) providing the necessary correlations, while the shared rotation parameters    │
│                          │ still let each qubit express independent-looking dynamics through phase differences       │
│                          │ generated by the entangling structure.                                                    │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0384                                                                                   │
