│                          │ layer), and replace the fixed CZ entangling ring with a parametrized CRZ ring using ONE   │
│                          │ shared parameter, giving the circuit trainable, but low-dimensional, entangling strength  │
│                          │ instead of no entangling parameter at all. This keeps the per-qubit RY layer (8 params,   │
│                          │ essential for individual feature encoding) but reduces the total distinct parameter count │
│                          │ from 24 to 11, which should reduce the train/val gap and improve worst-group margin,      │
│                          │ while adding a small amount of trainable entanglement expressivity that was previously    │
│                          │ absent (CZ was fixed).                                                                    │
