│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ none                                                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ The current ansatz uses 11 distinct trainable parameters (8 individual per-qubit RY       │
│                          │ angles plus 3 shared RZ/entangling params), giving a strong worst-group margin (0.11) but │
│                          │ a large train/val gap (0.24) and low parameter efficiency. Prior experiments show that    │
│                          │ reducing distinct-parameter count strongly increases the combined score even at some      │
│                          │ accuracy cost, and that entanglement depth can be increased "for free" by reusing the     │
│                          │ same shared parameter name on additional two-qubit gates (since the block is repeated     │
│                          │ with identical parameters).                                                               │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This edit collapses the 8 independent per-qubit RY angles into a 2-parameter even/odd     │
│                          │ alternating scheme (capturing input-dependent structure while drastically cutting         │
│                          │ parameter count), keeps single shared RZ pre/post phase parameters, and replaces the      │
│                          │ single-ring CRZ entangling layer with two shared-parameter entangling layers: a           │
│                          │ nearest-neighbor ring (including wraparound 7-0) and a skip-2 connectivity layer, both    │
│                          │ reusing the same "ent" parameter. This increases circuit connectivity/expressivity        │
│                          │ (useful for separating the hardest validation groups) without adding any new trainable    │
│                          │ parameters, going from 11 distinct params down to 5, which should reduce                  │
│                          │ overfitting/generalization gap and raise parameter efficiency while retaining reasonable  │
│                          │ margin.                                                                                   │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0589                                                                                   │
