│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ add_shared_zz_longrange                                                                   │
│ patch_description        │ The current ansatz suffers from a large train/validation gap (0.20), suggesting it        │
│                          │ overfits the small training set with only local nearest-neighbor entanglement. Adding a   │
│                          │ single shared long-range ZZ entangling layer between opposite qubits (0-4,1-5,2-6,3-7)    │
│                          │ before the local RY block injects global correlations with only one extra parameter. This │
│                          │ is inspired by the idea that disjoint, shared-parameter two-qubit Ising gates increase    │
│                          │ the effective feature space cheaply while acting as a form of regularization (fewer       │
│                          │ independent parameters covering more of the qubit topology), which should help close the  │
│                          │ generalization gap and improve the worst-group margin, at the cost of a small             │
│                          │ parameter-efficiency penalty (6 distinct params vs 5).                                    │
