│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ skip2_entangling_ring                                                                     │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the final fixed reversed-chain CNOT entangling layer with a "skip-2" ring         │
│                          │ topology that connects qubits at distance 2 (0→2→4→6→0 and 1→3→5→7→1). This creates       │
│                          │ longer-range, non-nearest-neighbor entanglement that mixes information across the         │
│                          │ register more thoroughly than a simple chain, while still using zero trainable            │
│                          │ parameters. The two independent skip-2 rings (even and odd qubits) also preserve a degree │
│                          │ of structured symmetry that may help generalization to harder validation groups,          │
│                          │ addressing the current high train/val gap by diversifying the entangling structure        │
│                          │ without adding parameters.                                                                │
