│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ merge_params_skip2_ring                                                                   │
│ patch_description        │ Two combined improvements: (1) reduce trainable parameter count from 6 to 4 distinct      │
│                          │ names by merging the previously split `ry_a`/`ry_b` and `rz_a`/`rz_b` rotation layers     │
│                          │ into single shared parameters `ry_ab` and `rz_ab` applied uniformly across all 8 qubits — │
│                          │ since parameter economy is explicitly rewarded at every count, this should directly raise │
│                          │ the score while keeping the same entangling structure and expressivity per qubit (each    │
│                          │ qubit still gets an input-encoding-dependent effect from a shared angle). (2) Replace the │
│                          │ second fixed entangling layer, which was just the reverse of the first nearest-neighbor   │
│                          │ CNOT chain (a redundant/adjacent topology), with a "skip-2" ring connecting qubits at     │
│                          │ distance 2 ([0,2],[2,4],[4,6],[6,0],[1,3],[3,5],[5,7],[7,1]). This creates two            │
│                          │ independent longer-range mixing cycles that combine with the nearest-neighbor chain and   │
│                          │ the distance-4 ZZ layer to give richer, more non-local entanglement coverage without      │
│                          │ adding any parameters, which prior evidence suggests improves robustness/generalization   │
│                          │ on the hardest validation groups.                                                         │
