│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ merge_ry_reduce_overfit_split_ent                                                         │
│ patch_description        │ The current spec uses 8 independent RY parameters (one per qubit) plus a single shared    │
│                          │ CRZ entangling parameter, yielding 11 distinct parameters and severe overfitting (train   │
│                          │ 0.94 vs val 0.72, gap 0.24). The two higher-scoring seed programs both used far fewer     │
│                          │ distinct parameters (4-5) with aggressive sharing of single-qubit rotations across all    │
│                          │ qubits, which generalized better and scored higher (0.39-0.41) despite lower train        │
│                          │ accuracy.                                                                                 │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This edit (1) collapses the 8 per-qubit RY parameters into a single shared "ry0"          │
│                          │ parameter (mirroring the successful seed-1 pattern), drastically cutting parameter count  │
│                          │ and combating overfitting, and (2) splits the single shared "ent" CRZ parameter into two  │
│                          │ parameters ("ent1" for even-indexed edges, "ent2" for odd-indexed edges) to retain some   │
│                          │ entangling expressivity/granularity at low added cost, similar to the recommended CRZ     │
│                          │ granularity refinement. Net distinct parameter count drops from 11 to 5, matching the     │
│                          │ best-performing seed's parameter budget while keeping the RZ pre/post structure intact    │
│                          │ for phase flexibility.                                                                    │
