│ patch_description        │ The best-performing prior variants used fewer distinct trainable parameters and showed    │
│                          │ smaller train/validation gap. The current candidate splits the RY and RZ rotation layers  │
│                          │ into two groups ("ry_a"/"ry_b" and "rz_a"/"rz_b"), doubling the parameter count relative  │
│                          │ to a fully-shared rotation layer, which likely hurts generalization (train-test gap 0.12  │
│                          │ vs 0.01-0.03 for lower-parameter seeds). This edit merges each split pair into a single   │
│                          │ shared parameter, cutting n_distinct_params from 6 to 4 while keeping identical gate      │
│                          │ structure (same entangling backbone, same ZZ layer, same CNOT rings), preserving          │
│                          │ expressivity per qubit (since each qubit still receives an input-dependent rotation)      │
│                          │ while reducing overfitting risk and improving parameter efficiency, which is heavily      │
│                          │ rewarded by the scoring function.                                                         │
