│ patch_description        │ Split the single shared CRZ entangling parameter "ent1" into two parameters "ent1a" and   │
│                          │ "ent1b", alternating along the linear chain (even-indexed edges use ent1a, odd-indexed    │
│                          │ edges use ent1b). This gives the entangling layer more expressive freedom to              │
│                          │ independently tune "even" vs "odd" bond phases, which can help separate                   │
│                          │ harder-to-classify sample groups that may respond differently to different parts of the   │
│                          │ chain, at the cost of only one extra trainable parameter (5 distinct total). This mirrors │
│                          │ the recommended finer-grained sharing strategy and should improve worst-group             │
│                          │ margin/robust separation while keeping parameter count low.                               │
