│ patch_description        │ Add a single shared long-range entangling layer (CRZ with one shared parameter "g") on    │
│                          │ opposite-qubit pairs [0,4], [1,5], [2,6], [3,7] before the existing RX(a)/RY(a) rotation  │
│                          │ layer. This seeds long-range correlations at the very start of the circuit at the cost of │
│                          │ just one extra trainable parameter, which prior evidence suggests substantially amplifies │
│                          │ the effectiveness of subsequent local rotations and ring entanglers for robust            │
│                          │ generalization on hard groups, without adding to circuit depth in a costly way (only 4    │
│                          │ gates).                                                                                   │
