│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ duplicate_block_shared_params                                                             │
│ patch_description        │ The current ansatz (ry_a/ry_b → ring1 → rz_a/rz_b → ring2 → ry_c) achieves reasonable     │
│                          │ train/val accuracy but the generalization gap is high (0.20) and score is lower than the  │
│                          │ simpler seed circuits. Following the recommendation, we duplicate the entire gate         │
│                          │ sequence back-to-back while reusing the exact same five parameter names (ry_a, ry_b,      │
│                          │ rz_a, rz_b, ry_c). This doubles the effective circuit depth (adding more entangling       │
│                          │ structure and expressive re-parametrized rotations) without increasing the trainable      │
│                          │ parameter count at all, since parameters are shared across the repeated block. Deeper     │
│                          │ circuits with fixed parameter budgets often improve the expressivity/generalization       │
│                          │ trade-off by allowing richer feature-map re-use (similar to data re-uploading /           │
│                          │ parameter-tying strategies), which can help reduce the train-test gap while maintaining   │
│                          │ separation on harder validation groups. Because n_distinct_params stays at 5, parameter   │
│                          │ economy is preserved, and since scoring rewards fewer distinct params strongly, this is a │
│                          │ low-risk way to test whether extra depth (without extra parameters) improves the          │
│                          │ worst-group margin and reduces the generalization gap.                                    │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0394                                                                                   │
│ error_attempt            │ None                                                                                      │
