                         Patch Metadata - Gen 28/80 - Novelty: 1/2 - Resample: 1/3 - Patch: 1/2                         
╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ add_crx_after_zz_entangler                                                                │
│ patch_description        │ The current ansatz uses a single parametrized ZZ(g) entangling layer on disjoint          │
│                          │ long-range pairs [0,4],[1,5],[2,6],[3,7]. To increase expressivity per parameter without  │
│                          │ adding much circuit depth, we insert a complementary parallel block of CRX(f) gates on    │
│                          │ the same four disjoint qubit pairs immediately after the ZZ(g) layer, sharing a single    │
│                          │ new parameter f. CRX gates entangle via a different generator (X-rotation conditioned on  │
│                          │ control) than the ZZ interaction (diagonal phase coupling), so combining them should let  │
│                          │ the circuit capture richer correlations between the same qubit pairs while only adding    │
│                          │ one new trainable parameter (n_distinct_params goes from 4 to 5, matching the             │
│                          │ best-performing seed configuration). Because the four CRX gates act on disjoint qubit     │
│                          │ pairs, they can be applied in a single parallel layer, keeping the depth increase minimal │
│                          │ (only +1) despite adding 4 gates. This mirrors the recommendation to complement           │
│                          │ phase-type entanglement (ZZ/CRZ) with rotation-type entanglement (CRX) using a shared     │
│                          │ parameter, aiming to reduce the train-test gap by giving the optimizer more flexible      │
│                          │ entangling structure without exploding parameter count.                                   │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0367                                                                                   │
│ error_attempt            │ None                                                                                      │
│ system_prompt_id         │ None                                                                                      │
│ model_name               │ openrouter/anthropic/claude-sonnet-5                                                      │
│ temperature              │ 1.0                                                                                       │
│ max_output_tokens        │ 16384                                                                                     │
│ diff_summary             │ added: 4; deleted: 0; modified: 0;                                                        │
