│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ none                                                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ Following the principle that fewer distinct trainable parameters strictly improves the    │
│                          │ score, this edit collapses the two alternating entangling parameters ("ent1"/"ent2") into │
│                          │ a single shared parameter "ent", and collapses the pre- and post-entangling RZ layers     │
│                          │ ("rz_pre"/"rz_post") into a single shared parameter "rz". This reduces the distinct       │
│                          │ parameter count from 5 to 3 while keeping the same gate structure, depth, and             │
│                          │ connectivity (RY ring, RZ layers, CRZ ring, skip-2 CNOT mixing, RZ layer), which          │
│                          │ previously already generalized well (near-zero gap). Sharing the RZ pre/post parameters   │
│                          │ imposes a symmetry constraint that acts as a regularizer, and sharing the CRZ ring        │
│                          │ parameter across all 7 ring edges gives a single global entangling strength, both of      │
│                          │ which should reduce overfitting risk on the small training set while preserving           │
│                          │ expressivity through the fixed skip-2 CNOT mixing layer.                                  │
│ num_applied              │ 3                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0420                                                                                   │
│ error_attempt            │ None                                                                                      │
│ system_prompt_id         │ None                                                                                      │
