│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ long_hop_entangler_4param                                                                 │
│ patch_description        │ Restructured the ansatz to use only 4 distinct trainable parameters (down from 5) while   │
│                          │ preserving strong bidirectional entanglement. The circuit now consists of: (1) a global   │
│                          │ shared RY rotation on all 8 qubits, (2) a fixed nearest-neighbor CNOT ring for local      │
│                          │ entanglement, (3) a global shared RZ rotation, (4) a fixed skip-2 "long-hop" CNOT         │
│                          │ entangler (0→2→4→6→0 and 1→3→5→7→1) that spreads correlations across non-adjacent qubits  │
│                          │ without adding parameters, (5) a single shared CRZ layer across four disjoint pairs to    │
│                          │ inject a small amount of parametrized entanglement, and (6) a final global shared RY      │
│                          │ rotation to consolidate the state before readout. This design reduces parameter count     │
│                          │ (improving parameter economy, which is weighted heavily), keeps depth in the previously   │
│                          │ effective ~40-45 range, and relies on fixed (non-parametrized) long-range CNOTs to build  │
│                          │ robust entangling structure that should generalize better than the deeper, more           │
│                          │ overfitting-prone variant that had 5 params and 0.20 generalization gap.                  │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0463                                                                                   │
