│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ split_crz_ring_dual_phase                                                                 │
│ patch_description        │ Currently the CRZ entangling ring in Layer 2 shares a single parameter "b" with the       │
│                          │ following CRX ring across all 8 edges, giving the model very coarse control over its      │
│                          │ phase-type entanglement pattern. Following the recommendation, we split the CRZ ring into │
│                          │ two independent phase parameters: even-indexed edges (0-1, 2-3, 4-5, 6-7) keep using "b"  │
│                          │ (still shared with the CRX ring, preserving most of the parameter economy), while         │
│                          │ odd-indexed edges (1-2, 3-4, 5-6, 7-0) now use a new parameter "d". This gives the ansatz │
│                          │ one extra degree of freedom to independently tune phase correlations on the two           │
│                          │ interleaved sub-rings, which should let it adapt its entangling profile more precisely to │
│                          │ the hardest validation groups while only increasing the distinct parameter count from 3   │
│                          │ to 4 — a small, well-justified cost given the potential robustness gain.                  │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0368                                                                                   │
