│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ none                                                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ The current ansatz uses a single CRZ ring (phase-type entangler) shared under the         │
│                          │ parameter "ent". Drawing on the insight from the first seed program that pairing a        │
│                          │ phase-type generator (CRZ) with an amplitude-type generator (CRX) under the SAME shared   │
│                          │ parameter substantially boosts expressivity-per-parameter without adding any new          │
│                          │ trainable parameters, I add a second ring of CRX gates on the same qubit pairs, reusing   │
│                          │ the "ent" parameter. This keeps n_distinct_params at 3 (no cost increase) while giving    │
│                          │ the entangling layer two independent rotation generators driven by one angle, which       │
│                          │ should improve separation on hard validation groups (worst-group margin) and robustness,  │
│                          │ since the circuit can now express both amplitude and phase correlations from a single     │
│                          │ scalar without extra parameter overhead.                                                  │
