│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ skip2_longhop_entangler                                                                   │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the second fixed CNOT chain (currently a reverse nearest-neighbor ring:           │
│                          │ [7,6],[6,5],[5,4],[4,3],[3,2],[2,1],[1,0]) with a skip-2 "long-hop" entangling pattern:   │
│                          │ CNOTs on [0,2],[2,4],[4,6],[6,0] and [1,3],[3,5],[5,7],[7,1]. This mirrors the topology   │
│                          │ already used successfully after the CRZ layer in an earlier seed program (which had a     │
│                          │ lower generalization gap), and increases qubit-connectivity diversity (each qubit now     │
│                          │ connects to a partner 2 hops away in both entangling stages) without adding any new       │
│                          │ trainable parameters. It also slightly reduces gate count (8 vs 7 CNOTs replaced by 8,    │
│                          │ roughly similar) while changing circuit topology to potentially improve robustness on the │
│                          │ worst-case validation group, since long-range correlations get mixed earlier in the       │
│                          │ circuit rather than purely local nearest-neighbor propagation twice in a row (forward     │
│                          │ ring then reverse ring is largely redundant).                                             │
