│                          │ 0.41, avoiding the costly duplicated-block structure that hurt depth and gap in the       │
│                          │ current 0.39 candidate), and apply the recommended refinement: split the final global     │
│                          │ RY(e) layer into two shared parameters — RY(e1) on qubits 0-3 and RY(e2) on qubits 4-7.   │
│                          │ This gives the circuit a small extra degree of freedom to model asymmetries between the   │
│                          │ two halves of the register while keeping the entangling structure and other rotations     │
│                          │ fully shared (only 1 extra distinct parameter versus the 0.41-scoring seed, and far fewer │
│                          │ parameters/depth than the current 0.39 candidate). The two-block duplication in the       │
│                          │ current file added parameters+depth without gain (score dropped to 0.39), so we prune it  │
│                          │ and instead invest the added capacity in the demonstrated-effective final-layer           │
│                          │ de-sharing.                                                                               │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Argumentation: the previous evaluation showed doubling depth by repeating the whole block │
│                          │ with shared params reduced val/test accuracy and combined score (0.41 -> 0.39), i.e. more │
│                          │ depth with the same parameters did not help generalization here — likely due to circuit   │
│                          │ becoming harder to optimize with the same expressivity but larger depth (more gate noise  │
│                          │ / barren-plateau-like effects). Splitting only the last readout-adjacent RY layer is a    │
│                          │ much cheaper, more targeted way to add expressivity exactly where it can sharpen the      │
│                          │ decision boundary, matching the given recommendation, without reintroducing the depth     │
│                          │ penalty.                                                                                  │
