│ patch_description        │ The current ansatz uses 5 distinct parameters (ry_a, ry_b, rz_a, rz_b, ry_c) and shows a  │
│                          │ large train/validation gap (0.81 vs 0.63, gap=0.20), indicating overfitting/high capacity │
│                          │ relative to the tiny training set. Since parameter economy is rewarded at every count and │
│                          │ reducing the generalization gap is explicitly valued, I merge the two alternating-qubit   │
│                          │ rotation layers (ry_a/ry_b and rz_a/rz_b) into single shared parameters each (ry_a,       │
│                          │ rz_a). This cuts the parameter count from 5 to 3 distinct trainable parameters while      │
│                          │ keeping the same gate structure/depth (same expressive entangling pattern), which should  │
│                          │ reduce overfitting, tighten the generalization gap, and improve parameter efficiency —    │
│                          │ all while preserving the diverse two-directional CNOT ring entangling structure that      │
│                          │ worked reasonably well.                                                                   │
