│ patch_name               │ none                                                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ The current candidate has no parametrized two-qubit gate at all, which the prior two seed │
│                          │ variants (both of which scored higher, 0.40-0.41) did have via a single shared CRZ        │
│                          │ entangling layer across disjoint pairs. Adding a light-weight, single-shared-parameter    │
│                          │ CRZ layer between the two CNOT rings introduces genuine entangling non-Clifford           │
│                          │ correlations (needed to separate hard groups) while adding only one extra distinct        │
│                          │ trainable parameter (6 total, matching the best-performing seed's parameter count). This  │
│                          │ should improve worst-group margin and reduce the current large train/val gap by giving    │
│                          │ the circuit a cheap way to encode pairwise correlations instead of relying purely on the  │
│                          │ alternating RY/RZ + CNOT-ring structure that appears to be overfitting (train 0.81 vs val │
│                          │ 0.63).                                                                                    │
