│ patch_description        │ Building on the current best-performing ansatz (4 distinct parameters, worst_group_margin │
│                          │ 0.04), this variant applies the recommended de-sharing of the final RY layer. Instead of  │
│                          │ a single shared RY(ry_c) across all 8 qubits, we split it into two shared parameters:     │
│                          │ RY(ry_c1) on qubits 0-3 and RY(ry_c2) on qubits 4-7. This gives the circuit a modest      │
│                          │ extra degree of freedom (5 distinct parameters total) to model asymmetries between the    │
│                          │ two qubit halves right before readout, which prior evidence suggests sharpens decision    │
│                          │ boundaries by a few percent while only mildly increasing parameter count (staying well    │
│                          │ within the parameter-economy constraints). All other structure (shared RY entry rotation, │
│                          │ fixed nearest-neighbor ring, shared RZ layer, fixed skip-2 ring, shared CRZ entangling    │
│                          │ layer) is kept identical to the current best design, since that combination already       │
│                          │ achieved the best worst-group margin and validation accuracy trade-off observed so far.   │
