│ patch_name               │ longhop_entangling_ring2                                                                  │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the second fixed offset CNOT ring (4 nearest-neighbor gates) with a long-hop CNOT │
│                          │ pattern that connects qubits at distance 2 in two interleaved rings ([0→2,2→4,4→6,6→0]    │
│                          │ and [1→3,3→5,5→7,7→1]). This introduces medium-range entanglement that nearest-neighbor   │
│                          │ rings miss, potentially capturing correlations relevant to the hardest validation groups, │
│                          │ while keeping the same parameter count (no new trainable parameters added) and staying    │
│                          │ within a reasonable depth/gate budget.                                                    │
