│ patch_name               │ none                                                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ The current candidate collapsed ry_a/ry_b and rz_a/rz_b into single shared parameters and │
│                          │ dropped the CRZ entangling layer entirely, which regressed the score from 0.42 to 0.39    │
│                          │ (lower validation accuracy and margin). This edit restores the higher-performing          │
│                          │ structure from the earlier generation (separate ry_a/ry_b and rz_a/rz_b parameters plus   │
│                          │ the shared CRZ(ent) layer on disjoint pairs), which is known to reach 0.42. On top of     │
│                          │ that, following the recommendation, we insert a parallel CRX(f) layer immediately after   │
│                          │ the CRZ(ent) layer using the same disjoint pairs [0,1],[2,3],[4,5],[6,7] with a new       │
│                          │ shared parameter f. This enriches the non-Clifford entangling structure at very low       │
│                          │ parameter cost (only 1 extra distinct parameter), which should improve robust separation  │
│                          │ on harder validation groups while keeping parameter count economical (7 distinct params   │
│                          │ total).                                                                                   │
