│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ none                                                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ The current low-parameter ansatz (3 distinct params) achieves a low score (0.39) despite  │
│                          │ fewer parameters, largely because the fixed CNOT rings provide no trainable phase         │
│                          │ structure and the model under-fits the harder validation groups. The best-performing      │
│                          │ prior variant (0.42) used more distinct parameters but had a stronger entangling          │
│                          │ structure. To recover expressive entangling capability while keeping the parameter count  │
│                          │ as low as possible, we replace both fixed CNOT rings with parameterized CRZ ("controlled  │
│                          │ phase") gates on the same wire connectivity, sharing a single new parameter "h" across    │
│                          │ all of them. This turns the previously untrainable entangling rings into a single extra   │
│                          │ trainable phase parameter, giving the optimizer a lever to tune inter-qubit correlation   │
│                          │ strength without adding coherent bit-flip noise sensitivity from CNOTs, and only costs 1  │
│                          │ extra distinct parameter (4 total), which should still register as parameter-efficient    │
│                          │ while substantially improving worst-group margin and generalization.                      │
│ num_applied              │ 2                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0357                                                                                   │
