│ patch_description        │ This candidate merges the two strongest prior designs. From the high-scoring "ry_a/ry_b   │
│                          │ split" ansatz we keep the alternating‑wire RY encoding layers (odd/even split), the       │
│                          │ forward‑then‑backward CNOT entangling chain, and the disjoint‑pair CRZ entangler with a   │
│                          │ single shared parameter, all of which produced the best validation margin and worst‑group │
│                          │ margin (0.42 score). From the parameter‑economical current program we adopt the idea of   │
│                          │ collapsing the two separate RZ layers (rz_a/rz_b) into a single shared "rz" parameter,    │
│                          │ cutting one more distinct parameter while preserving the same circuit topology and depth  │
│                          │ of information mixing. The result keeps the effective entangling/rotation structure that  │
│                          │ generalizes well (alternating single-qubit encoding, bidirectional nearest-neighbor       │
│                          │ entanglement, then disjoint-pair parametrized entanglement, then a global closing         │
│                          │ rotation) but with only 5 distinct trainable parameters (down from 6), which the scoring  │
│                          │ function rewards directly through parameter efficiency while retaining the good margin    │
│                          │ properties of the higher-scoring parent circuit.                                          │
