├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ phase_entangling_rings                                                                    │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the two parameter-free CNOT ring passes (forward 0→7 and reverse 7→0) with        │
│                          │ parametrized CRZ (phase-type) entangling rings that share a single new parameter "h".     │
│                          │ Bit-flip (CNOT) entanglers can be more sensitive to encoding noise and tend to scramble   │
│                          │ amplitude information; phase-type entanglers (CRZ) preserve more of the encoded amplitude │
│                          │ structure while still creating full entanglement across the ring, which should improve    │
│                          │ generalization to harder validation groups. Although this adds one new distinct           │
│                          │ parameter, the resulting boost to worst-group margin and robustness is expected to        │
│                          │ outweigh the small parameter-count penalty, and depth/gate count remain unchanged.        │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
