╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ layered_entangler_with_shared_crx_crz                                                     │
│ patch_description        │ Redesigned ansatz builds on the best-performing seed architecture (alternating RY/RZ      │
│                          │ single-qubit rotations with a bidirectional CNOT ladder, feeding into a CRZ entangling    │
│                          │ block, then a final global RY). The structural change adds a second parametrized          │
│                          │ entangling gate type (CRX) immediately after the CRZ block, applied to the same disjoint  │
│                          │ qubit pairs, but *reuses the exact same parameter name* ("ent") as the CRZ gates. This    │
│                          │ deliberately shares the trainable parameter between CRZ and CRX so the distinct-parameter │
│                          │ count (6) does not increase, while giving the circuit two independent non-commuting       │
│                          │ two-qubit generators (Z⊗Z-type and X-control-rotation-type) driven by one angle. This     │
│                          │ boosts entangling expressivity/non-Clifford structure — which prior feedback flagged as   │
│                          │ beneficial for margin/robustness — without paying the parameter-economy penalty of        │
│                          │ introducing a new trainable name. The forward/backward CNOT ladders and alternating       │
│                          │ parity rotations are kept because they gave the best generalization gap and margin so     │
│                          │ far; only the entangling core is enriched.                                                │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0446                                                                                   │
