│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ none                                                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the two fixed, non-parametrized CNOT entangling rings with parametrized CRZ gates │
│                          │ that all share a single new parameter "h". This turns pure bit-flip (CNOT) entanglers     │
│                          │ into phase-type entanglers (akin to the CZ-ring recommendation, but using CRZ since CZ    │
│                          │ cannot carry a trainable parameter in this gate set). Sharing one parameter across all 12 │
│                          │ gates keeps the parameter-count increase to just +1 distinct parameter while adding       │
│                          │ meaningful trainable entangling structure, which should improve robustness/generalization │
│                          │ (phase interactions are typically less sensitive to bit-flip-like noise and can better    │
│                          │ shape the decision boundary) without harming the strong parameter-economy priority.       │
│ num_applied              │ 2                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0416                                                                                   │
│ error_attempt            │ None                                                                                      │
