│ patch_name               │ add_shared_crx_layer_after_crz                                                            │
│ patch_description        │ Add a CRX entangling layer immediately after the existing CRZ(d) block, using the SAME    │
│                          │ parameter name "d" as the CRZ gates (parameter sharing) so that no new distinct trainable │
│                          │ parameter is introduced. This adds an extra non-Clifford two-qubit entangling operation   │
│                          │ (CRX) that mixes X-basis correlations complementary to the existing Z-basis CRZ           │
│                          │ entanglers, which can increase expressivity and improve robust separation on hard         │
│                          │ validation groups without increasing parameter count (keeping n_distinct_params at 5,     │
│                          │ only adding depth/gate count). This follows the recommendation to insert a CRX layer for  │
│                          │ boosted entanglement while respecting the strong preference for parameter economy by      │
│                          │ reusing the existing "d" parameter instead of introducing a new one.                      │
