│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ add_crx_entangler_after_crz                                                               │
│ patch_description        │ The current ansatz uses only a phase-type (CRZ) entangling layer shared via a single      │
│                          │ parameter "ent". This limits the entangling operation to diagonal (Z-basis) correlations, │
│                          │ missing amplitude-mixing (X-basis) correlations that could help separate                  │
│                          │ harder-to-classify groups. I add a parallel CRX layer immediately after the existing CRZ  │
│                          │ entangler, on the same disjoint pairs (0,1),(2,3),(4,5),(6,7), sharing a single new       │
│                          │ parameter "crx_ent". This is a minimal addition (+1 distinct parameter, +4 gates, +1      │
│                          │ depth) that introduces non-diagonal two-qubit rotations, increasing the expressive power  │
│                          │ of the entangling block without significantly increasing overfitting risk, since the      │
│                          │ parameter is fully shared. This should help boost the worst-group margin (the dominant    │
│                          │ score term) by giving the circuit richer entangling structure to fit hard-to-separate     │
│                          │ samples, while keeping the parameter count increase minimal.                              │
