│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ split_entangler_even_odd                                                                  │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the current chain-style ansatz with the higher-performing block-diagonal          │
│                          │ structure from the best prior seed (RY_a/RY_b -> CNOT ring -> RZ_a/RZ_b -> reverse CNOT   │
│                          │ ring -> CRZ(ent) pairs -> final RY_c), which previously scored 0.42 vs the current 0.40.  │
│                          │ Additionally apply the suggested refinement: split the shared "ent" CRZ parameter into    │
│                          │ two group-specific entanglers — "ent_e" for even-indexed pairs [0,1] and [4,5], and       │
│                          │ "ent_o" for odd-indexed pairs [2,3] and [6,7]. This gives finer-grained control over even │
│                          │ vs. odd neighbor correlations at the cost of only one extra parameter (7 distinct total), │
│                          │ which prior evidence suggests tightens the decision boundary and improves worst-group     │
│                          │ margin/validation accuracy while keeping parameter count low.                             │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0504                                                                                   │
