│ patch_description        │ The duplicated two-block variant (current file) actually hurt generalization (score       │
│                          │ dropped from 0.42 to 0.39) relative to the single-block version with a CRZ entangling     │
│                          │ layer. Revert to that better single-block structure, and add a parallel CRX entangling    │
│                          │ layer immediately after the CRZ layer, reusing the SAME shared parameter name ("ent")     │
│                          │ instead of introducing a new one. This adds amplitude-mixing (CRX) on top of the existing │
│                          │ phase-mixing (CRZ) for extra non-Clifford expressivity and better separation of hard      │
│                          │ groups, while keeping the distinct parameter count unchanged (6 params total), which      │
│                          │ strongly favors the score per the parameter-economy criterion. Depth increases only       │
│                          │ modestly (+4 gates), a low-risk way to boost worst-group margin without growing           │
│                          │ train-test gap.                                                                           │
