│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ none                                                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ The current EVOLVE-BLOCK (using a/b/c shared params) underperformed (0.40) relative to    │
│                          │ the earlier seed structure (0.42) that used parity-broken RY encoding, a forward/backward │
│                          │ CNOT sandwich, a shared CRZ ring entangler, and a final shared RY readout with 6 distinct │
│                          │ parameters. I restore that stronger structural pattern, but additionally merge the two    │
│                          │ separate RZ phase parameters (rz_a, rz_b) into a single shared "rz_ab" parameter to free  │
│                          │ up parameter budget. This lets me append the recommended concluding global RZ("rz_out")   │
│                          │ layer after the final RY readout — giving an extra adjustable phase "twist" right before  │
│                          │ measurement to sharpen class separation — while keeping the total distinct parameter      │
│                          │ count at 6, matching the best-performing prior seed's economy. This should combine the    │
│                          │ higher validation/worst-group margins of the proven structure with the sharper decision   │
│                          │ boundary from the extra readout phase, without increasing parameter cost.                 │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
