                         Patch Metadata - Gen 63/80 - Novelty: 1/2 - Resample: 1/3 - Patch: 1/2                         
╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ none                                                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ Two complementary changes aimed at (1) reducing parameter count, which the scoring rule   │
│                          │ rewards unconditionally, and (2) tightening the margin on the hardest validation group by │
│                          │ adding a symmetric mid-circuit phase-alignment layer that reuses an existing shared       │
│                          │ parameter rather than introducing a new one.                                              │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. Merge the long-range `zz_h` coupling into the same shared parameter as the short-range │
│                          │ ring coupling `zz_g`. This cuts the number of distinct trainable parameters from 6 to 5   │
│                          │ while keeping the same entangling connectivity (nearest-neighbor ring + opposite-half     │
│                          │ long-range links), letting the optimizer find one consistent entangling strength that     │
│                          │ generalizes better instead of two independently-tunable ones that can overfit the small   │
│                          │ training set.                                                                             │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 2. Insert a symmetric RZ layer on every qubit using the already-existing `rz_c`           │
│                          │ parameter, placed right after the long-range ZZ coupling and immediately before the final │
│                          │ closing RY rotation. This creates a two-phase phase-alignment (RZ before entangling, RZ   │
│                          │ after entangling, same parameter) analogous to the balanced RY/RZ sandwiching seen in     │
│                          │ higher-scoring variants, without adding any new trainable parameter, which should help    │
│                          │ align phases picked up by the two ZZ layers and tighten the worst-group margin.           │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0367                                                                                   │
│ error_attempt            │ None                                                                                      │
│ system_prompt_id         │ None                                                                                      │
│ model_name               │ openrouter/anthropic/claude-sonnet-5                                                      │
│ temperature              │ 1.0                                                                                       │
│ max_output_tokens        │ 16384                                                                                     │
│ diff_summary             │ added: 13; deleted: 0; modified: 4;                                                       │
