│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ none                                                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ The current ansatz already overfits strongly (train_acc=1.00 vs val_acc=0.78, gap=0.31)   │
│                          │ despite only 6 distinct parameters, and per the scoring rules fewer distinct trainable    │
│                          │ parameters always score higher. I merge the two symmetry-broken initial RY rotations      │
│                          │ (ry_a/ry_b) into a single shared parameter, and reuse the same rotation-angle parameter   │
│                          │ (zz_g) for the long-range ZZ coupling instead of introducing a separate zz_h. This        │
│                          │ reduces the parameter count from 6 to 4 distinct names while keeping the same gate        │
│                          │ structure/depth (so entangling power and expressivity per layer is preserved), which      │
│                          │ should shrink the train/validation gap, improve robustness on the hardest validation      │
│                          │ groups, and directly boost the parameter-economy term of the score.                       │
