│ patch_description        │ The current candidate underperforms (score 0.39) despite having fewer parameters, likely  │
│                          │ because the final RY layer leaves residual phase correlations unexploited before readout. │
│                          │ Following the recommendation, we append a disjoint ZZ-Ising layer (paired on              │
│                          │ (0,1),(2,3),(4,5),(6,7)) immediately after the final shared RY rotation, using a single   │
│                          │ new shared parameter "zz_out". This is a minimal-depth (+1), non-Clifford entangling      │
│                          │ block that can sharpen decision margins by coupling readout-adjacent qubit pairs, similar │
│                          │ to how the CRZ entangling layer benefited the earlier-scoring seed (0.42). This only adds │
│                          │ one distinct trainable parameter (n_distinct_params: 5->6), which is a modest cost given  │
│                          │ the potential margin/generalization gains, and keeps circuit depth low.                   │
