│ patch_name               │ single_block_rz_split                                                                     │
│ patch_description        │ The duplicated two-block ansatz (current program, score 0.39) doubles depth/gate-count    │
│                          │ while reusing all parameters, which caused severe underfitting (train_accuracy dropped to │
│                          │ 0.56) — the extra depth without new parameters likely pushed the circuit into a           │
│                          │ barren-plateau-like regime. Revert to the single-block structure that previously scored   │
│                          │ highest (0.42), which keeps depth/gate-count moderate and retains the CRZ entangling      │
│                          │ term. On top of that, apply the recommended refinement: split the mid-circuit "rz_a"      │
│                          │ parity term into "rz_a0" (wires 0,4) and "rz_a1" (wires 2,6) while leaving "rz_b" on the  │
│                          │ odd wires unchanged. This gives finer phase-alignment granularity in the middle of the    │
│                          │ circuit at the cost of only one extra distinct parameter (7 total instead of 6), which    │
│                          │ should improve worst-group margin and validation accuracy without reintroducing the       │
│                          │ depth-related generalization collapse seen in the duplicated version.                     │
