│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ mixed_axis_entangling_reuse_param                                                         │
│ patch_description        │ The current ansatz applies four disjoint CRZ gates all sharing parameter "d" for its      │
│                          │ entangling layer, which only rotates in the Z-basis and may limit the correlations the    │
│                          │ classifier can express per parameter. Building on the recommendation to mix entangling    │
│                          │ axes, I convert two of the four CRZ gates (on pairs [2,3] and [6,7]) into CRX gates while │
│                          │ keeping them tied to the SAME shared parameter name "d" (rather than introducing a new    │
│                          │ "ent_x" parameter). This gives the circuit access to both Z-axis and X-axis controlled    │
│                          │ correlations from a single trainable angle, increasing expressivity per parameter without │
│                          │ increasing the distinct parameter count (still 5), which is important since parameter     │
│                          │ economy is scored strongly. This should help recover generalization/robustness lost in    │
│                          │ the current variant while respecting the "fewer distinct params always better" guidance.  │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0334                                                                                   │
