│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ none                                                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ The current ansatz uses two independent parameters (ry_a_0, ry_a_1) for the diagonal      │
│                          │ even-qubit subgroups, which raises the distinct-parameter count to 7 without a clear      │
│                          │ margin benefit (worst_group_margin actually dropped vs. the simpler shared-parameter seed │
│                          │ that scored higher). Since parameter economy is weighted heavily and monotonically in the │
│                          │ score, merging these two into a single shared parameter "ry_a" (matching the proven       │
│                          │ high-scoring seed's even-qubit design) reduces the distinct parameter count from 7 to 6   │
│                          │ while preserving the overall circuit structure, depth, and entangling topology. This      │
│                          │ should improve parameter efficiency and likely improve generalization (smaller effective  │
│                          │ parameter space, less overfitting risk) without harming the expressive entangling ZZ      │
│                          │ layers that provide the actual separation power.                                          │
