│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ prepend_disjoint_xx_block                                                                 │
│ patch_description        │ The current candidate collapses to essentially a shallow, low-expressivity circuit        │
│                          │ (train_acc 0.62, worst_group_margin ~0.00), showing that with only 3 distinct parameters  │
│                          │ the circuit cannot build enough separation even on the training set. To inject stronger,  │
│                          │ structured entanglement at minimal parameter cost, I prepend a disjoint-pair XX-Ising     │
│                          │ layer (wires (0,1),(2,3),(4,5),(6,7)) sharing a single new parameter "xx_a" before the    │
│                          │ initial RY layer. This creates early two-qubit correlations across all qubits with just   │
│                          │ +1 distinct parameter (4 total), which should substantially increase the achievable       │
│                          │ margin/separation while keeping parameter economy strong (this mirrors the recommendation │
│                          │ and is a minimal, well-motivated way to add non-Clifford entangling capacity without      │
│                          │ exploding parameter count).                                                               │
