│ patch_description        │ The current low-parameter ansatz (3 distinct params) underfits badly (train acc 0.62,     │
│                          │ worst-group margin negative), showing it lacks enough expressivity to separate the        │
│                          │ hardest samples even on the training set. To add expressive power with minimal parameter  │
│                          │ cost, we insert a shared ZZ-Ising entangling layer on disjoint qubit pairs right after    │
│                          │ the CNOT butterfly block and before the final RZ layer. This introduces genuine Z-Z       │
│                          │ correlations across the register (complementing the existing CRZ chain and CNOT           │
│                          │ permutation) using a single new shared parameter "zz_mid", raising the distinct parameter │
│                          │ count from 3 to only 4 while giving the circuit more capacity to build separable decision │
│                          │ boundaries, which should improve both training fit and worst-group margin without a large │
│                          │ parameter-efficiency penalty.                                                             │
