│ patch_description        │ The previous edit path (ZZ/CRX long-range coupling with shared params) regressed          │
│                          │ performance (0.40) compared to the earlier seed using a bit-reversal CNOT ladder with a   │
│                          │ CRZ entangling layer (0.42). We revert to that stronger-performing seed structure and     │
│                          │ apply the recommended mixed-axis entangler refinement: instead of four identical CRZ      │
│                          │ gates, keep CRZ on pairs [0,1] and [4,5] (renamed "ent_z") while switching pairs [2,3]    │
│                          │ and [6,7] to CRX (new shared parameter "ent_x"). This preserves the depth/gate-count      │
│                          │ profile of the higher-scoring seed while injecting complementary X-Z entangling couplings │
│                          │ that may better capture non-Clifford correlations needed for the harder validation        │
│                          │ groups, at the cost of one extra distinct parameter (7 vs 6), which should still be a     │
│                          │ good trade given the substantial score gain of the base structure.                        │
