│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ mixed_axis_entangler_crx_crz                                                              │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the uniform CRZ entangler (single shared "ent" parameter across all four qubit    │
│                          │ pairs) with a mixed-axis pattern: pairs [0,1] and [4,5] keep CRZ under a renamed shared   │
│                          │ parameter "ent_z", while pairs [2,3] and [6,7] become CRX under a new shared parameter    │
│                          │ "ent_x". This injects complementary Z- and X-basis couplings into the entangling layer,   │
│                          │ which should let the circuit capture correlations that a single rotation axis cannot      │
│                          │ express, potentially improving the worst-group margin and robustness on held-out data.    │
│                          │ Gate count and depth are unchanged since we only swap gate type on two of the four        │
│                          │ entangling pairs and split one shared parameter into two shared parameters (a modest,     │
│                          │ well-justified increase in trainable parameter count from 6 to 7 distinct parameters,     │
│                          │ traded for expected gains in separation robustness).                                      │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
